# Bench baseline. Refresh whenever optimise/import internals change
# (rerun the exact commands below, replace numbers, note the machine).
# Regressions are judged against this file, not against memory.

machine: i5-14600KF (20 threads), ext4, linux 7.1.5-arch1-1
date: 2026-07-27

"interleaved" below = alternate two built prefixes run by run through
one bench binary (LD_LIBRARY_PATH picks the library, as bench-ab.cc
does), min of 8 pairs. Use it for anything under ~15%: noise bursts
here land on whole runs, and measuring A then B charges the burst to
whichever side it hit. A plain 5-run median called one change
anywhere from 3% to 25%.

Host numbers cannot see the source medium (see bench/vm-commit.sh):
they dump a page-cache-warm tree, a box reads compressed squashfs.
That difference reversed one verdict below.

